[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)):
"the desk merges on subject alone; nobody has to read the body." Reading cause instead of
subject splits it into two bugs with two different fixes.

<Callout kind="warn">
Filing one ticket per cause here, each with its count. #4471 stays open for the one cause
that is actually its majority cause; the other gets a ticket of its own below.
</Callout>

## What's actually in here

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table above is this page's only source of these numbers — it runs the same
`causes.ts` logic live against `reports-4471.json` and `desk-notes.json`, the same way the
original #4471 page does. Nothing below is typed in by hand. Two causes, two tickets — no
more: `desk-notes.json`'s `oneDayMove` footnote (5 of the 379 under `parser`) reads oddly
in the body, but the kb's own cause logic files it under `parser` same as the rest, so it
stays inside that one ticket rather than a third of its own.

## The two tickets

1. **[Parser flips month/day](https://github.com/tomaszlis/firstrepo/issues/1)** — the
   shared parser reads every date month-first, flipping it for every day-first-locale
   tenant on `app`/`email` and on `booking-v2` forms. This is `#4471`'s real, majority
   cause — the row the table above marks as this ticket's own. 379 reports, including the
   5 `oneDayMove`-footnoted ones. **Fixed** — `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
2. **[Wrong form hint on booking-v3](https://github.com/tomaszlis/firstrepo/issues/2)** —
   a different bug, same-looking symptom: three tenants on `booking-v3` see a
   `MM/DD/YYYY` hint despite being day-first locales. Channel-specific (`form` only),
   so it can't be the shared parser. The table marks this cause `wrong` for `#4471`: "not
   this ticket — no ticket of its own," until now. 33 reports. **Won't fix** —
   `booking-v3` form retired.

Per the desk's engineering update on #4471, closed 05 Oct.

## Lesson

Subject-line dedupe is fast and that's the right trade during an incident
([triage](/kb/triage/dedupe) says so, and it's still right). But "known: one issue, one
fix queued" was true of the subject line, not of the reports. A ticket this size is worth
one pass through `causes.ts` before the fix ships — the signal was already sitting in the
channel column the desk already collects.

